  "practice": [
    "Say অ three times with its short inherent sound: ô, ô, ô.",
    "Read each vocabulary word aloud and notice অ at the beginning or as the built-in vowel sound of a consonant.",
    "Contrast অ (ô) with আ (a): অল্প (ôlpo), আম (am).",
    "Read কম aloud as kôm and notice that the অ sound is present even though অ is not visibly written."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "অ is the first independent vowel in the Bengali alphabet and is commonly transliterated as ô.",
    "অ is often present as the built-in vowel sound of a consonant even when it is not visibly written. For example, কম is approximately kôm.",
    "Recognizing this inherent vowel is one of the keys to becoming comfortable reading Bangla.",
    "Keep অ distinct from the longer আ sound. Compare অল্প (ôlpo, a little) with আম (am, mango)."
  ]
